# help, a built-in (roadmap os-server.md P12): the built-ins, the programs
# and the keys. On all three emulators: DOSBox-X's shell starts in /, as it
# cannot read the drives (docs/emulators.md), so it goes there first.
program: sh
emulators: bochs mame dosbox-x
keys: cd /\nhelp\n
---
rx286, test build
@bochs /a$ cd /
@mame /a$ cd /
@dosbox-x /$ cd /
/$ help
Built in:  cd [DIR], pwd, exit [STATUS], export NAME=VALUE, unset NAME, set,
           alias NAME=VALUE, unalias NAME, jobs, fg [%N], bg [%N], true,
           false, help
Files:     ls [-l], cat, head [-n N], wc, cp, mv, rm, mkdir, rmdir, more,
           lp (to the printer), echo
Processes: ps [-e], kill [-SIGNAL] PID, sleep SECONDS, env [NAME=VALUE] [CMD]
Machine:   date [+FORMAT], uptime, clear, keys, mem, fpu, crash KIND, spin
Devices:   beep, play, joy, mouse, term (COM2)
Lines:     CMD | CMD, CMD; CMD, && ||, & (in the background), < > >> 2>
Keys:      Backspace, Up and Down (the last lines), ^C (stop), ^Z (stop a
           job), ^D (the end), Alt+F1 to F8 (the terminals)
/$
